# November 22, 2026: a first scatter across Michigan, the state with the fewest places on the map (24, all but one in
# Marquette County). Ground claimed with tools/choose.py --thinnest. Places spread over the Keweenaw, the eastern Upper
# Peninsula, the Straits, the Lower Peninsula's west side, the Thumb, Detroit, Marshall, Monroe and Saginaw.
# Sources read in this session: Wikipedia articles and county Register lists (tools/wiki_raw.py), and the pages of
# whoever runs each place: the Keweenaw County Historical Society, the Quincy Mine Hoist Association, the Calumet
# Theatre, the Michigan History Center, the Hiawatha National Forest, the Great Lakes Shipwreck Historical Society,
# Mackinac State Historic Parks, the Menominee Range Historical Foundation, Port Huron Museums, Michigan Central,
# the City of Detroit and the Historic Fort Wayne Coalition, the Marshall Historical Society, the National Park Service
# and the Castle Museum. Interiors were not visited by any source opened unless the entry says so.
from data_b import N
